  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0087 database is used for storing information about customers, subscriptions, receipts, and users/teams. The customers table contains information about individual customers, including their ID, billable ID, billable type, trial end date, and updated and created dates. The subscriptions table contains information about customer subscriptions, including their ID, billable ID, billable type, name, Paddle ID, Paddle status, Paddle plan, quantity, trial end date, paused from date, and ends at date. The receipts table contains information about customer receipts, including their ID, billable ID, billable type, Paddle subscription ID, checkout ID, order ID, amount, tax, currency, quantity, receipt URL, paid at date, updated, and created dates. The users/teams table contains information about users and teams, including their ID. The customers, subscriptions, and receipts tables have foreign keys referencing the users/teams table, which ensures referential integrity. The foreign keys are set to cascade on update and delete, which means that if a user or team is deleted, their related customers, subscriptions, and receipts will also be deleted. The schema also includes primary keys and unique constraints to ensure entity integrity.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a component of the Laravel ecosystem, specifically focusing on integrating the Cashier package with Paddle's subscription billing services. Laravel Cashier Paddle serves as an abstraction layer, offering a streamlined API for Laravel applications to manage Stripe and customer subscriptions, including recurring billing operations.\n\n 2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to provide a fluent interface that simplifies the management of subscription billing within Laravel applications. This includes basic and advanced subscription management features, reducing the overhead of writing subscription billing code.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Individuals or teams using Laravel to build applications that require subscription billing functionality.\n- End Users: Customers who will interact with the subscription services indirectly via applications utilizing this package.\n- Business Owners: Organizations aiming to leverage subscription-based business models.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Subscription Management: Enable the creation, updating, and cancellation of customer subscriptions.\n- Subscription Swapping: Allow customers to switch between different subscription plans.\n- Quantity Management: Manage the quantities associated with customer subscriptions.\n- Subscription Pausing: Provide options to pause and resume subscriptions, with grace periods as needed.\n- Receipts: Generate and store transaction receipts with relevant details such as amounts, taxes, and currency.\n- Data Linking: Utilize a database schema to track customers, subscriptions, and receipts while maintaining referential integrity through foreign keys.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Usability: The API should be intuitive and offer a fluent interface to reduce the complexity of billing operations for developers.\n- Scalability: The system should efficiently handle a large number of customers and transactions.\n- Reliability: Ensure data consistency and integrity within the database, especially concerning billing operations.\n- Security: Protect sensitive customer data and secure transactions using industry-standard practices.\n- Performance: Optimize for quick response times when performing billing operations.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0087.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0087\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `billable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `billable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `trial_end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customers_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`billable_id`) REFERENCES `users_teams` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `subscriptions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `billable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `billable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `paddle_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `paddle_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `paddle_plan` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `trial_end_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `paused_from_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ends_at_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `subscriptions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`billable_id`) REFERENCES `users_teams` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `receipts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `billable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `billable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `paddle_subscription_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `checkout_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `tax` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `currency` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receipt_url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `paid_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `receipts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`billable_id`) REFERENCES `users_teams` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users_teams` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
